'' A UDT THAT EXTENDS A STRING: THE BASE IS A MARKER, NOT STORAGE, AND THE WIDE
'' CONVERSIONS GO THROUGH THE CAST.
''
'' Two independent defects, both in tests/vendor/fbc-tests/udt-wstring/conversion.bas,
'' whose UWSTRING_FIXED_BASE is 'extends wstring'.
''
'' THE CONVERSION. The narrow rows of the VAL family have asked "is this a UDT that
'' casts to a string" since they were written; the WIDE branch did not. 'cint( u )'
'' over a type declaring 'operator cast( ) byref as const wstring' compared the OBJECT
'' to zero -- 'icmp ne [34 x i8] %t7, 0', which is not an instruction, so clang refused
'' the module. ONLY WHEN IT EXTENDS WSTRING, for the reason the narrow side gives: the
'' cast alone is fbc's error 20, so accepting it would answer a program fbc refuses.
''
'' THE LAYOUT. Measured, fbc:
''
''     type C extends wstring : x as byte : end type    sizeof 1
''     type D extends zstring : x as byte : end type    sizeof 1
''
'' -- the base occupies NOTHING and contributes no alignment either. What it buys is
'' that the string family's conversions accept the type at all. tiko counted it as the
'' 2 (or 1) bytes a bare wstring or zstring reports, so every such type was too long
'' and every field after the base sat at the WRONG OFFSET. Six MIR goldens held that,
'' and all six programs differential clean against fbc after the change -- they had
'' never been built.
''
'' Differenced against fbc: '32 / 123 / true / 32' and then '1 1'.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/udt-extends-wstring.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered

'' THE WIDE VAL ENTRY POINTS, reached through the cast rather than over the aggregate.
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_WstrValLng
'' GOLDEN: expected/udt-extends-wstring.out
